+    },
+    "first_broken_contract": "arnold_pipelines.megaplan.orchestration.task_splitter.split_high_complexity_tasks removes a finalized task ID but publishes neither a typed replacement map nor a reference-closed payload; downstream consumers therefore observe identifiers outside the transformed task set.",
+    "missed_backstop": "Finalize has no single pre-publication task-reference-closure assertion across graph, critique custody, validation coverage, sense checks, and user-action fields. Feasibility validates only dependency edges, task_feasibility.json can be written before late custody rejection, and the circuit-open route fails to persist the latest_failure/resume_cursor required by its own recover-blocked next step.",
+    "canonical_owner": "Megaplan finalize contract owner: orchestration/task_splitter.py transform, handlers/finalize.py mutation/publication order, orchestration/task_feasibility.py and critique_custody.py consumers, graph_admission/control_interface circuit transition, and Run Authority/Custody/WBC recovery admission.",
